#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "b3be2b13-b455-5dde-accf-259c075e1e1f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4350" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105520 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/id #uuid "c6f2dacc-11b0-5689-97d9-e1869c64aae1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4351" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "4deee6cc-69e4-5da4-9c78-57bf6c988500" :question/math-academy-id "e-4352" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc8ae94-2946-54bd-aff9-b44c313314b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304790} {:answer/id #uuid "e9542f1b-d2f9-5ac0-bfe0-3203017e4fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304791} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6415a9-b093-5db7-bd13-83682a0bfe5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304792} {:answer/id #uuid "21d53ddb-de51-560c-85bf-881912effa65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304793} {:answer/id #uuid "e17d943d-4bbd-5582-a671-9c76b195af36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9542f1b-d2f9-5ac0-bfe0-3203017e4fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304791} :answer-field/id #uuid "12fcbdbf-0e6d-5e4f-8997-9e5ade5ecd7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8addc76a-7a22-5ce6-a1e9-a31f1d8601cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-128433" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨0,-1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,9,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,7,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+(3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 2)+4(3\\cdot 7-2\\cdot 9) \\\\  & =14+12 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|26|=26.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304795 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "975a10d8-e0f9-5167-b382-47e92eb34088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304797} {:answer/id #uuid "0b9914a3-6baf-52f5-b2b7-3c9ee7144a72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304798} {:answer/id #uuid "291a9c56-c12a-54ce-b94a-8ec1c044442d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304799} {:answer/id #uuid "01db86c0-0f6a-5292-8cd0-6a439b395459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304800} {:answer/id #uuid "06de81d2-3e21-557f-9a3a-8ac7735e68bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975a10d8-e0f9-5167-b382-47e92eb34088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304797} :answer-field/id #uuid "47d5fb1f-490d-55ae-985d-d4129fc0807b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fee03e2-7b8b-52e8-9d97-0baaa37f0e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-128436" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨8,0,3⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,1,1⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3)-(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 3)+4(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-3k+1+32 \\\\  & =33-3k \\\\  & =3(11-k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 3(11-k) & =0 \\\\ 11-k & =0 \\\\ k & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5974393-f829-54d7-91c0-fd587e068758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304804} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8ebb7d-8cfe-5e1a-9279-0d0387a22fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304805} {:answer/id #uuid "9067da6b-8493-5f3b-9b68-fa205658e970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304806} {:answer/id #uuid "ba52d37c-beed-5d26-a1ba-0857c8944a99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304807} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b9bfc3-cbb1-58a9-95b6-31444cb48ce5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9067da6b-8493-5f3b-9b68-fa205658e970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304806} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1bbef33-f5ce-5ddc-8847-26d5714921f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fcdb30c1-0274-5980-b4e4-6f085a9d2d9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128454" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨t,t,1⟩,$ $q=⟨3,2,6⟩,$ and $r=⟨3,4,0⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}t & t & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|-t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t(2\\cdot 0-4\\cdot 6)-t(3\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 6)+(3\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-24t+18t+6 \\\\  & =-6t+6 \\\\  & =6(1-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 6(1-t) & =0 \\\\ 1-t & =0 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cfa2bc6-5c0c-5f60-9b63-5b21f19aa303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304811} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea4754b-fbac-5bfd-b185-8be3aac498f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304812} {:answer/id #uuid "6d97a031-cc6c-52aa-be70-921941b546af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304813} {:answer/id #uuid "092d5576-ea50-5550-a39c-f663112cd5b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304814} {:answer/id #uuid "43e468c9-e10b-5db2-9815-c8ef1e40ef19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43e468c9-e10b-5db2-9815-c8ef1e40ef19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304815} :answer-field/id #uuid "5520fe93-05f4-505b-ae92-4e2eb9ba5950" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf4e15d3-e811-5a46-a65f-cf81e20caa0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-128456" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $a=⟨3,-1,7⟩,$ $b=⟨t,4,t⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,6,8⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 7 \\\\ t & 4 & t \\\\ 2 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & t \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & t \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(4\\cdot 8-6\\cdot t)+(t\\cdot 8-2\\cdot t)+7(t\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =96-18t+8t-2t+42t-56 \\\\  & =30t+40 \\\\  & =10(3t+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 10(3t+4) & =0 \\\\ 3t+4 & =0 \\\\ t & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=-\\frac{4}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3882ae5f-2c77-5f2a-b003-368de5ef9d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304818} {:answer/id #uuid "095180c4-959a-5657-9cc5-bd7ffdecbfce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304819} {:answer/id #uuid "b4dafd37-ab0e-5b3b-aaf4-7139bb13cc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304820} {:answer/id #uuid "92bb3cf0-98e0-5849-9c53-b7052aef9ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304821} {:answer/id #uuid "da76ed50-63d4-53ab-9c44-0169c6546b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3882ae5f-2c77-5f2a-b003-368de5ef9d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304818} :answer-field/id #uuid "6455940b-7783-5ded-9621-05e5ec5fcb74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9c9d6569-3b77-597b-a21a-9122b96a9702" :question/math-academy-id "q-128475" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(7,6,4),$ $B(8,5,9),$ $C(7,4,2),$ and $D(5,7,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(8i+5j+9k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =i-j+5k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,5⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(7i+4j+2k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(5i+7j+4k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i+j \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-2))+(0\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot (-2))+5(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2-4-20 \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-22|=22.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "683f85c0-e9db-5d85-84b7-55f69a5b3486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304825} {:answer/id #uuid "ede45f4c-2489-5ed7-ada0-f196db5efd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304826} {:answer/id #uuid "6529f215-8f69-5482-82bd-ce51ddb1ea39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304827} {:answer/id #uuid "a5eceaa9-fbe3-526e-8603-a89d2dd2add5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304828} {:answer/id #uuid "c8abb60a-5d81-5853-9f64-304d9fd7a02c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ede45f4c-2489-5ed7-ada0-f196db5efd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304826} :answer-field/id #uuid "795a48b4-5676-5a87-ac80-15e711d27746" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "05303239-00ac-5a68-9122-d90f8f4b7f26" :question/math-academy-id "q-128483" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(5,1,4),$ $B(4,1,7),$ $C(3,1,5),$ and $D(2,3,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+j+7k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+j+5k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+3k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-3i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1)-0+3((-2)\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2-12 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-10|=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef5ebf59-6fe5-59ef-a3d3-b0c347a63905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304832} {:answer/id #uuid "39d7c572-9876-5c6c-83ec-04cbeb3e08a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef5ebf59-6fe5-59ef-a3d3-b0c347a63905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304832} :answer-field/id #uuid "839829d8-fa02-5da6-a1dd-b573f71f9cd3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0744b7bb-a8e1-5df9-b653-93a21c6bbd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-280670" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $y=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, and $z=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1-4-6 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc6584b-c0bc-57a9-b4d5-4d22eb1408b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dc6584b-c0bc-57a9-b4d5-4d22eb1408b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304836} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4f4255f-3833-5828-a63e-9a1bcecb322c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9f96834-1106-564c-99a3-d27a34e4432f" :question/math-academy-id "q-280671" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,1,2⟩$, $y=⟨-3,2,0⟩$, and $z=⟨4,-2,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-2))-1((-3)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 4)+2((-3)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2+3-4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|1|=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "350d9b2d-aa3e-59e7-8823-92d269c2526a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "350d9b2d-aa3e-59e7-8823-92d269c2526a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304839} :answer-field/id #uuid "326f34d7-f92d-5bdf-aaf4-3a2306ca71ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17caabc4-9097-5667-a511-683b71910128" :question/math-academy-id "q-280712" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,5,0⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(30)-2(0)+3(-20) \\\\  & =30-0-60 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-30|=30.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7ae065c-9983-515b-8e9e-90f69bf3a6b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7ae065c-9983-515b-8e9e-90f69bf3a6b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304842} :answer-field/id #uuid "248c54ac-e12c-53fa-84e3-ec4be7225ed9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3604cd4-a926-5c59-82f0-a8b6a0116615" :question/math-academy-id "q-280716" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $x=⟨3,1,4⟩$, $y=⟨0,2,5⟩$, and $z=⟨6,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 0)-(0\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 6)+4(0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =6+30-48 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-12|=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b0c600a-692f-5e3a-b25e-fdd0ee2c7aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b0c600a-692f-5e3a-b25e-fdd0ee2c7aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304845} :answer-field/id #uuid "27995133-2c1e-5a9f-8688-c9730e7e9250" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9ff91b8-84da-5141-aa19-31035dc9f26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280729" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,k,k⟩$, $b=⟨0,3,2⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & k & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|-k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 0)-k(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 4)+k(0\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =15+8k-12k \\\\  & =15-4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 15-4k & =0 \\\\ 4k & =15 \\\\ k & =\\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{15}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28e6f2fe-da70-5b2a-903b-f9ccae9614e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28e6f2fe-da70-5b2a-903b-f9ccae9614e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304848} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeb0e33e-239e-5c78-9cc0-bd378ee4d355" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "526b6b57-f2db-5e13-aa9a-c9b02b118080" :question/math-academy-id "q-281029" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,1,3),$ $B(0,5,5),$ $C(3,4,5),$ and $D(2,0,2).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5j+5k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =4j+2k \\\\  & =⟨0,4,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+5k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+2k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+2k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =2i-1j-1k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4(3\\cdot -1-2\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot -1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =28-18 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304849 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b421de7-6ce3-531e-ab76-200c91231136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b421de7-6ce3-531e-ab76-200c91231136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304851} :answer-field/id #uuid "9987a9a4-b325-596d-b143-3f3c5385e5c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90129f6e-2010-58a8-9c15-bbe333617408" :question/math-academy-id "q-281030" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(-1,0,1),$ $B(2,-3,4),$ $C(-2,-2,2),$ and $D(0,-1,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-3j+4k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =3i-3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-2j+2k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+1k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-j+5k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-8+1)+3(-4-1)+3(1-(-2)) \\\\  & =-21-15+9 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-27|=27.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6757763-e497-5a8a-b9ce-1220ee0be9dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304854} {:answer/id #uuid "d05dae85-1862-5809-ba43-8634551789ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304855} {:answer/id #uuid "3610979b-bfb2-5834-93d9-03136e19fb14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304856} {:answer/id #uuid "d251522f-691b-5326-b3d1-13d6990e2508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304857} {:answer/id #uuid "8809a18e-993c-523b-8fae-7e827b70dc16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d251522f-691b-5326-b3d1-13d6990e2508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304857} :answer-field/id #uuid "46e94a93-6e10-5b23-909b-64979d9d21b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af998713-889e-5171-8ee6-d3189c58c418" :question/math-academy-id "q-73735" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨0,3,6⟩$, $q=⟨t,t,2⟩$, and $r=⟨-1,2,7⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ t & t & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}|+6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & t \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(t\\cdot 7-(-1)\\cdot 2)+6(t\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot t) \\\\  & =-21t-6+12t+6t \\\\  & =-3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ -3t-6 & =0 \\\\ -3t & =6 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b25ce2c-4da6-5e6d-bbb7-340c9413bec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304861} {:answer/id #uuid "282453a2-b2e6-5d81-853e-fa20abce6943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304862} {:answer/id #uuid "24a3e20f-f690-571d-9053-654de5f647b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304863} {:answer/id #uuid "adfd7320-70ed-5358-bcde-d53cfd58b4df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304864} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc84eeb-2226-5348-8b91-8ce8e69d39c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "282453a2-b2e6-5d81-853e-fa20abce6943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304862} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c8dabc3-dee7-552a-9a50-6e8a3420977b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bab47f92-25ef-577c-a8d1-c6370f94e260" :question/math-academy-id "q-73745" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,-1,2)$, $B(-2,2,3)$, $C(1,1,1)$, and $D(-1,3,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+2j+3k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j+k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-i+3j-2k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+4j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot (-4)-4\\cdot (-1))-3(0\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot (-1))+(0\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12+6+4 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|22|=22.\n$$"}]}
